<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Aspilos	    unloading   corn screening  6,018     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn gluten     2,855</p>
<p>Volgobal 148     unloading   barley	    2,740     Europe</p>
<p>Kezelsk	     1/7	  sunflower meal  2,354     Europe</p>
<p>Bodaybo	     1/7	  feed wheat	2,700     Europe</p>
<p>Kaptan Yilmas     2/7	  sunflower meal  1,520     Europe</p>
<p>Ruja		  3/7	  feed wheat	1,600     Europe</p>
<p>Arnaki		7/7	  corn	     24,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  29,950</p>
<p>				     soya	     13,804</p>
<p>Matheus	     8/7	  wheat	    37,500     U.S.</p>
<p>				     gluten meal     6,900</p>
<p>				     gluten feed    13,700</p>
<p>Flag Nicolas     10/7	  corn	     23,524     U.S.</p>
<p>				     barley	    8,400</p>
<p>Volgobalt 186    10/7	  bran wheat	2,400     Europe</p>
<p>Liberty Wave     12/7	  n/a		60,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Ganza		29/7	  corn + soya    22,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					pellets +</p>
<p>					sunflower meal</p>
<p>Paragon	     1/8	  corn	     19,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  12,100</p>
</text>
